menu "Tiercel board"

    config TIERCEL_KNOB_INVERT
        bool "Invert knob direction"
        default n
        help
            Swap clockwise and anticlockwise. The knob's A contact is wired as
            clockwise on the Waveshare 1.8" module; set this only if a unit
            turns the wrong way.

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_FORCE_ERM
        bool "Skip LRA calibration and drive the motor as an ERM"
        default n
        help
            The motor is an LRA (LRA_P/LRA_N on the schematic). At power-up
            the DRV2605 auto-calibrates it and plays effects closed loop,
            falling back to ERM open loop only if calibration fails. Enable
            this to always use ERM open loop, as Waveshare's demo does --
            clicks are then too faint to feel through the glass.

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_LRA_RATED
        int "LRA rated voltage (RATED_VOLTAGE register)"
        range 16 255
        default 80
        help
            Closed-loop target amplitude, about 20.7 mV rms per step at
            ~200 Hz: 80 is roughly 2 V rms, typical for a coin LRA. Raise it
            for a stronger feel, lower it if the motor rattles.

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_LIBRARY
        int "DRV2605 waveform library"
        range 1 7
        default 5
        help
            Used only on the ERM fallback (the LRA path always uses library
            6). 1-5 are ERM libraries, 7 is the 4.5V ERM library. 5 is what
            Waveshare's demo selects.

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_OD_CLAMP
        int "Motor drive clamp (OD_CLAMP register)"
        range 64 255
        default 166
        help
            The peak voltage the DRV2605 drives the motor with, in steps of
            21.59 mV (ERM open loop): 166 is about 3.6 V, so the output
            saturates at the board's supply. The chip's power-on value is 140
            (3.0 V), which leaves every effect noticeably weaker -- too light
            to feel through the glass. Lower it if a unit buzzes harshly.

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_DETENT_EFFECT
        int "Effect for a knob detent"
        range 1 123
        default 1
        help
            Played on every detent that moves a selection or a value: the
            lightest kind, one short click. 1 is "Strong Click 100%" -- the
            shorter, softer ticks (21-26) cannot be felt through the glass.

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_TAP_EFFECT
        int "Effect for an accepted tap"
        range 1 123
        default 10
        help
            Played when a tap selects or opens something: two clicks, one up
            from a detent. 10 is "Double Click 100%".

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_CONFIRM_EFFECT
        int "Effect for a committed change"
        range 1 123
        default 12
        help
            Played when something takes effect -- a device toggles, a mode is
            set: three clicks. 12 is "Triple Click 100%".

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_BACK_EFFECT
        int "Effect for going back"
        range 1 123
        default 14
        help
            Played when a swipe, a hold or the back chip takes you back a
            screen. 14 is "Strong Buzz 100%": long enough to feel under a
            finger still pressing the glass, and unlike any click, so back
            never feels like a selection.

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_LIMIT_EFFECT
        int "Effect for a knob value at its limit"
        range 1 123
        default 52
        help
            Played on every extra detent once a knob-adjusted value is at its
            minimum or maximum. 52 is "Pulsing Strong 1 100%", which no other
            kind uses, so an end stop never reads as a detent.

    config TIERCEL_HAPTIC_ALERT_EFFECT
        int "Effect for an alarm"
        range 1 123
        default 47
        help
            47 is "Buzz 1 100%".

endmenu
